# Where the production build fetches sector tiles from. Sector tile sets are
# data and ship from their own repo through jsDelivr, not from this one (see
# "Publishing tiles" in CLAUDE.md); this file is what makes a local
# `npm run build` produce the same app CI deploys, instead of one that throws
# for every set too big to live in public/.
#
# The ref stays `@main`. What moves when tiles are re-cut is the set hash in
# the folder name, so a new cut arrives as a new folder under this same
# prefix. A ref that moved instead would make every tile a device already
# holds unknown to the service worker's prune, and re-download the lot.
#
# Dev is not this file: `npm run dev` serves tiles from public/ on its own
# origin, and `?tiles=<url prefix>` points them at a set that is not published
# yet. Setting VITE_TILE_ORIGIN in the environment overrides this value.
VITE_TILE_ORIGIN=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/azabrod1/moon-tiles@main
